{
  "_comment": [
    "The offline map, sized for a 2.5 GB package. Run it with fetch-maps.cmd, or:",
    "    bin/tile_prefetch --plan assets/config/offline-map-plan.json --cache assets/maps --dry-run",
    "",
    "Three tiers, all contiguous from level 0 so that nothing has a hole the",
    "viewer would have to stop refining at:",
    "  globe  - every tile on Earth to level 6, both layers: the planet from space",
    "  land   - every tile with land in it, imagery and relief to 9, tapered:",
    "           Mercator tiles shrink toward the poles, so each level stops where",
    "           the one above already has the equator's ground resolution - level",
    "           9 to 60 degrees, 8 to 75, 7 to 83. The same detail on every",
    "           continent; the oceans stay at level 6",
    "  detail - mountain ranges (relief to 11 and imagery to 10 over 95 km,",
    "           imagery to 11 within 50 km of each one's heart), airports and",
    "           cities (imagery to 14, relief to 12), and flight corridors",
    "           (imagery to 11)",
    "",
    "Elevation is stored at 128 x 128 in whole metres (elevationSize): the mesh",
    "draws 64 x 64 of it and the DEMs are good to metres, so it costs a quarter",
    "of what it is served as, for nothing on screen.",
    "",
    "Outside the detail regions, land imagery is 306 m per pixel at the",
    "equator and no coarser anywhere. See assets/config/maps.README.md for",
    "what that looks like and what larger budgets buy."
  ],
